comments.body:
@dkmsoft It's basically not a real problem and Milos and all the other developers have lot's of other important things to do as well. I really appreciate all the effort put into AndroidAPS and the fact it's made available for everyone.

I made a quick fork (as a temporary workaround) with disabled Warning. Please keep in mind that you are using it at your own risk. It's based on AndroidAPS 3.0.1, I only disabled the yellow warning. Here's the fork: [Link to the AndroidAPS Fork without warning](https://github.com/maheini/AndroidAPS/tree/AndroidAPS_3.0.0.1_disabled_ic-baseline-warning). Feel free to build your AndroidAPS from this fork.

Maybe I'll even find the time & solution to create a real fix.
